dered":true,"items":["A Step"]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"items":["Substeps can be nested indefinitely deep."]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"items":["A Final Step"]}]},{"type":"section","heading":"Index terms","level":1,"body":[{"type":"paragraph","text":"In the simplest case, index terms consists of just a <primary> element, but  they can also consist of a <primary> and <secondary> element, and  can even include a <tertiary> term."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Index terms can also refer to other index terms: exclusively, using the <see> tag; or  as a reference to related terms, using the <seealso> tag."},{"type":"paragraph","text":"Nested content in index term elements is flattened."}]},{"type":"section","heading":"Abbreviated title","level":1,"body":[{"type":"code","text":"  { <code> }"}]}]}
